WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.382
Now we move from variable names to data types.

00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:10.177
A data type tells Python what kind of value it is working with and what operations make sense.

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:12.482
An integer is a whole number.

00:00:12.482 --> 00:00:14.722
A float includes a decimal.

00:00:14.722 --> 00:00:19.653
A string represents text. A Boolean stores True or False.

00:00:20.297 --> 00:00:25.669
The meaning matters. Twelve visits is naturally an integer because it is a count.

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:30.454
Nineteen point ninety-nine is a float when it represents a price.

00:00:30.454 --> 00:00:34.874
A city name is text, and an active flag is Boolean.

00:00:34.874 --> 00:00:41.264
Before calculating with any value, think about what it represents—not just what it looks like.
